      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5a995d0bbf71f62789f7311d|full_name}: I don't think it's good idea, as you don't want to see that menu when you interact with items. Even thru now days people spend time on front of mirror or video player not interacting, keep in mind that VRChat suppose to be interactive and with scripting system coming in it will be even more important aspect. It need to seamless and interactive by default, so sort of kind of toggle when you don't want to interact would be better imo. Or maybe different button for sitting since chairs are main source of annoyance.\n\nUltimate solution for that would be enforcing sitting range on chairs, but it too late for that as it would break compatibility with already existing worlds.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-12-26T17:40:22.421Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Players often accidentally activate or grab objects in worlds. The most common thing I've seen is sitting in chairs unintentionally or switching into an avatar when trying to use a gesture that involves grabbing.\n\nSome way of toggling these interactions or otherwise disconnecting it from gestures would prevent this kind of accidental avatar swapping or sitting in chairs. This would be especially useful given the new avatar stations on avatars making chairs more common. \n\nAn alternative to a toggle might be a more complex button combination for activating or grabbing objects that is less easy to trigger accidentally when performing gestures.\n\nThanks!\n(I could not find a duplicate/related issue but if one exists please let me know and I'll delete this)",
